<div class="nx-hero-wrap">
  <section class="nx-container nx-hero">
    <div class="nx-hero-copy">
      <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="nx-pill"><b>v2.8.0</b>See what is new</a>
      <h1 class="nx-title">The Python framework for the whole web app.</h1>
      <p class="nx-lead">
        Ship pages, an API and interactive parts from one project. Your team keeps Python, and
        your frontend keeps the tools it likes.
      </p>
      <div class="nx-actions">
        <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-primary">Read the docs</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-ghost">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="nx-art">
      <img src="/hero-light.svg" alt="The Nexy mark above three stacked pages" class="nx-art-light" width="640" height="560" />
      <img src="/hero-dark.svg" alt="The Nexy mark above three stacked pages" class="nx-art-dark" width="640" height="560" />
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="nx-sep-wrap">
  <section class="nx-container nx-sep">
    <div class="nx-sep-inner">
      <span>Nexy</span>
      <span class="nx-sep-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>FastAPI</span>
      <span class="nx-sep-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Vite</span>
      <span class="nx-sep-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Python</span>
      <span class="nx-sep-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>TypeScript</span>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="nx-container nx-section">
  <h2 class="nx-h2">Less glue, more product.</h2>
  <p class="nx-sub">A web app is a server, a router, a frontend and the work of connecting them. Nexy ships them already connected.</p>
  <div class="nx-bento">
    <article class="nx-tile nx-tile-wide">
      <span class="nx-icon nx-icon-server" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h3>Python on the server, all the way</h3>
      <p>Routes, validation, data and background work stay in the language your team already knows. There is no second backend to build, host and keep in sync.</p>
      <div class="nx-tile-visual">
        <div class="nx-chips">
          <span class="nx-chip">Pages</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">API</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Validation</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Database</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Background work</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="nx-tile nx-tile-narrow">
      <span class="nx-icon nx-icon-frontend" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h3>Any frontend, only where it helps</h3>
      <p>Pages are plain HTML and ship no framework. Add the one you like when a screen needs it.</p>
      <div class="nx-tile-visual">
        <div class="nx-chips">
          <span class="nx-chip">React</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Vue</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Svelte</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Solid</span>
          <span class="nx-chip">Preact</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="nx-tile nx-tile-narrow">
      <span class="nx-icon nx-icon-bolt" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h3>Fast from the first save</h3>
      <p>The page updates as you type. A mistake shows up in the page, with the code around it, not buried in a log.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nx-tile nx-tile-wide">
      <span class="nx-icon nx-icon-shield" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h3>Ready for production</h3>
      <p>Security headers are on, server actions check where a request comes from, and one build runs anywhere Python runs.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="nx-container nx-band-wrap">
  <section class="nx-band">
    <h2 class="nx-h2">Build your next product on Nexy.</h2>
    <p class="nx-sub">Free, open source and MIT licensed.</p>
    <div class="nx-actions">
      <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-primary">Read the docs</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-ghost">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
